<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Forest Bathing and Other Biohacks – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 10px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Managing Stress in Changing Times</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Forest Bathing and Other Biohacks</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Describe a personal achievement. Interactive: Engage in storytelling sessions using personal experiences.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can describe personal achievements related to managing stress (e.g., "Practicing mindfulness has helped me stay calm during stressful times.")<br>Can engage in storytelling by sharing personal experiences in managing stress and describing techniques like mindfulness (e.g., "Walking in the Metropolitan Natural Park is a peaceful way to manage stress for me.")<br>Can answer questions about personal stress management practices, using examples to illustrate their effectiveness (e.g., "Listening to calming music helps me focus before exams.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; background-color: #f2f2f2;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification. This stage activates prior knowledge and introduces the lesson's focus.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a collage of images showing various stress-management activities (e.g., someone practicing deep breathing, a person walking in a forest, listening to music, doing yoga, exercising). Students work in pairs to discuss which images they find most calming or effective, using phrases like, "<i>In my experience, walking in nature helps with focus</i>," or "<i>Listening to calming music helps me relax</i>." The teacher encourages them to use vocabulary from previous lessons such as <i>relaxation, mindfulness, exercise, nature, soothing, peaceful, calming</i>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models sharing a personal experience and giving advice using the target grammar. For example: "Last week, I felt overwhelmed before a big meeting. <i>Practicing deep breathing for 5 minutes really helped me focus</i>. You <i>should try</i> finding a quiet spot to meditate when you feel stressed." The teacher explicitly models the pronunciation of the long vowel sound /uː/ in words like "soothing" and "smooth," and the alternation of full and reduced vowels in multisyllabic words such as "mindfulness" and "beneficial."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of key terms and grammar structures.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say '<i>Practicing mindfulness helps</i>,' what is 'practicing'?" (Is it an action or a thing? - An action used as a noun, a gerund.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I tell you, '<i>You should try forest bathing</i>,' am I giving you an order or a suggestion?" (A suggestion/advice.)</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Managing Stress in Changing Times". This stage provides authentic language input.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio clip (approx. 1.5-2 minutes) of two Panamanian teenagers discussing their personal stress management "biohacks" and recent achievements in staying calm. The dialogue will include gerunds (e.g., "<i>Attending Zumba classes has helped me reduce stress</i>"), modals for advice (e.g., "<i>You could try deep breathing</i>"), and present continuous for trends (e.g., "<i>People are practicing forest bathing more these days</i>"). It will feature vocabulary like <i>forest bathing, relaxation, techniques, focus, beneficial, quiet spot</i>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interacting verbally to express ideas, feelings, and opinions on personal wellness strategies and achievements, using appropriate language for social interaction and a respectful tone.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students listen to the audio twice.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions (after first listening):</b> "What are the two speakers mainly discussing?" "What kind of strategies do they mention?" (e.g., <i>stress management, relaxation techniques</i>)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching (after second listening):</b> Students match each speaker to one specific stress management technique they mentioned (e.g., Speaker A - <i>attending Zumba classes</i>, Speaker B - <i>finding a quiet spot for meditation</i>).</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking. Students practice using the new language with guidance.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice using gerunds to describe activities, modals for giving advice, and the present continuous for trends, incorporating vocabulary such as <i>mindfulness, deep breathing, forest bathing, meditation, wellness, beneficial, soothing, manage, reduce, improve</i>.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice - Sentence Completion (Oral):</b> The teacher provides sentence stems on the board or projector, and students orally complete them in pairs, focusing on correct gerund formation and modals. Example stems:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"_____ (practice) mindfulness has helped me stay calm." (<i>Practicing</i>)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"You _____ (try) spending time in nature." (<i>should try</i>)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"_____ (listen) to calming music is a great technique." (<i>Listening</i>)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"People _____ (practice) biohacks to improve their wellness." (<i>are practicing</i>)</li>
                        </ul>
                        The teacher monitors and provides immediate feedback on pronunciation, particularly for words with /uː/ and multisyllabic stress.
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice - Advice Chain:</b> Students form small groups (3-4). One student states a common stressor (e.g., "I feel overwhelmed before exams."). The next student politely offers advice using a modal and a gerund (e.g., "<i>You could try listening</i> to calming music before exams. <i>It helps me focus</i>."). The third student can add another suggestion or describe a personal experience (e.g., "<i>Practicing deep breathing is beneficial for me</i>."). This continues around the group. The teacher emphasizes a respectful tone and the use of diverse vocabulary related to stress management techniques.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction - 'Ask a Biohacker':</b> Students work in pairs. Student A acts as a "stress consultant" and Student B is a "client" seeking advice. Student B describes a stressful situation they're experiencing (e.g., "I'm having trouble sleeping because of schoolwork."). Student A asks questions about their current habits and then offers suggestions for managing stress politely, using gerunds, modals, and linking to personal experience if applicable (e.g., "<i>Have you considered meditating</i> in a quiet spot? <i>In my experience, finding a serene place to relax promotes balance</i>."). They switch roles after 2-3 minutes.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Managing Stress in Changing Times". Focus on fluency and communicative task completion.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: 'My Stress Management Story' Storytelling Session</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students will work in groups of three. Each student will prepare a short personal story (1-2 minutes) about a time they successfully managed stress using a specific biohack or technique. They should describe the situation, the technique used, and the positive outcome (personal achievement). The story must include:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least two gerunds (e.g., "<i>Practicing yoga helped me reduce stress</i>").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least one modal for advice (e.g., "<i>You should consider incorporating deep breathing</i> into your daily routine.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Relevant vocabulary (e.g., <i>relaxation, forest bathing, mindfulness, beneficial, calming, relief, focus</i>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clear pronunciation of words with /uː/ and appropriate stress in multisyllabic words.</li>
                </ul>
                After each student tells their story, the other group members will ask 1-2 follow-up questions, offering polite suggestions or sharing similar experiences (e.g., "<i>That sounds like a helpful technique! Have you ever thought about trying forest bathing for additional relief?</i>"). The focus is on engaging in interactive storytelling and sharing personal wellness strategies respectfully.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy to check understanding and application.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy: Teacher Observation Checklist & Peer Feedback</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher uses an observation checklist to note student performance during the storytelling session, focusing on the evaluation criteria. Additionally, students provide structured peer feedback using a simple form with specific criteria.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students perform their "My Stress Management Story" storytelling session in their groups. The teacher circulates, listening to interactions and story content.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation (especially /uː/ and multisyllabic words).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate and appropriate use of target vocabulary (nouns, verbs, adjectives).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct use of gerunds and modals for advice.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence in describing personal achievements and experiences.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Active engagement in collaborative interaction (asking/answering questions, offering suggestions politely).</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a brief exit ticket:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new stress management technique I learned about today is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I feel confident using _____ (gerund/modal) to give advice/describe an achievement." (Students fill in the blank).</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Consolidation of learning and planning for future lessons.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of sharing your stress management story did you find most challenging, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can you apply the advice and techniques discussed today to your own life or to help others?"</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What speaking strategies or activities worked particularly well for promoting fluency and interaction? What specific pronunciation difficulties were observed, and how can they be addressed in future lessons? Were students able to use gerunds and modals for advice accurately and spontaneously? What adjustments or additional scaffolds (e.g., more sentence frames, focused pronunciation drills) are needed for students who struggled with expressing their ideas clearly or using the target grammar?</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Lesson 4: Writing), students will build upon their oral storytelling skills by writing about their personal stress management achievements and advising others. This will involve transforming their spoken narratives into coherent written paragraphs, focusing on structure, grammar, and vocabulary accuracy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>